WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:04.571
- The best Box 'Em Up story
happened to Brian Urlacher.

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:08.341
- I can't believe you got him.
- The best. The greatest one.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:10.343
We created this game
that was called Box 'Em Up

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:12.979
because everybody got,
like, Nike and Reebok shoes

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:14.848
and different things
and clothes

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:16.816
and then you'd have the boxes,
the cardboard boxes left over.

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:19.219
So people would be walkin', and
if they're not payin' attention

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:21.554
you just run up behind 'em
and slam a box over their head

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:22.989
and say, "Box 'em up!"

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.424
So everybody had to have

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:26.326
their head on a swivel
in the locker room.

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:27.927
So Brian was really good

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:29.763
at getting other people, too,
cuz he's sneaky.

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:31.998
Like, he'd get you comin' out of
your meeting room or something

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:34.567
and, boom, you got a box
slammed over your head.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.436
He would get so many people
that, yeah

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:38.238
everybody kinda
had it out for him.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:40.373
- Everybody turned on him.
He was the box bully.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:42.542
- Yeah. It only took me once.
You get boxed on once——

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:44.110
- You got the head
on a swivel.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.945
- Like, literally,
around the locker room

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:47.781
you got your back to the wall.
- [Laughing]

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:50.183
- I'm keepin' everybody
in front of me.

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:52.185
I think the D-line
brainstormed on, like

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:54.387
"What would be the best way
to try to get him?"

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:56.089
And, I mean, it was brilliant.

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:58.725
- I'm imagining the D-line
doing, like, a space shuttle launch.

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:02.028
- Yeah, they probably had,
like protractors and
all kind of stuff.

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:03.563
You know, it's Urlacher,
so you gotta get him.

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:05.065
- Yes, right.
- I don't know

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:07.534
how they got this box, but
it was like a six-foot box.

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:11.104
And in our locker room, there's
stairs to go to the second floor

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:12.806
where all the cardio stuff is

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:14.974
and there's a platform,
so you can't see who's up there.

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.643
So he comes out, and so right when

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:19.145
he walks out from
under the platform

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.948
somebody drops that six-foot box
right on his head.

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:24.150
He had his arms down.
It dropped, like,
straight over him.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.586
He's like, "Ahhh! Ahhh!
I'm stuck in the box!"

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:28.655
And he's, like, trying
to get it off of him.

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:30.323
Everybody's like,
"Box 'em up!"

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:31.791
All you saw was
two little feet, like

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:34.160
kickin' out of the box
and stuff.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.830
- [Laughing]
- That's awesome.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:37.263
This is a special moment for me.

